<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Inkwell — Home</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="shell">
      <!-- ========== top bar ========== -->
      <header class="topbar">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <span class="brand__mark">✒</span>
          <span class="brand__name">Inkwell</span>
        </a>

        <nav class="nav">
          <a class="nav__link nav__link--active" href="/">Home</a>
          <a class="nav__link" href="/blogs">Blogs</a>
          <a class="nav__link" href="/compose">Compose</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <!-- ========== hero ========== -->
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="hero__kicker">A tiny blog, built by hand</p>

        <h1 class="hero__title">
          Write it
          <span>down</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="hero__lede">
          No drafts, no dashboards, no distractions. Type a title, type a
          thought, hit publish. Everything you write lands on the blogs page,
          newest first.
        </p>

        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/compose">Start writing</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/blogs">Read the blog</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========== latest posts ========== -->
      <section class="section-head">
        <h2>Latest</h2>

        <!-- TODO (student) — post count
             Replace the hardcoded "0 posts" below with the real number.
             The route that renders this page should pass a `posts` array,
             so print its length here, followed by the word "posts". -->
        <span class="section-head__count">0 posts</span>
      </section>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — show the 3 most recent posts

        1. Wrap the <li class="post"> block below in a loop over `posts`.
        2. Only the first 3 should show here (slice the array in the route,
           or stop the loop after index 2 — your call).
        3. Fill in the real values:
             .post__index   -> the loop counter, starting at 1
             .post__title   -> the post's title
             .post__meta    -> the author inside <b>, then the created date
             .post__body    -> a short preview of the content
                               (first ~120 characters is plenty here)
        4. Delete this sample card once your loop renders real data.
      -->
      <ul class="post-list">
        <li class="post">
          <div class="post__top">
            <span class="post__index">1</span>
            <h3 class="post__title">Sample post title goes here</h3>
          </div>

          <p class="post__meta">By <b>Author name</b> · Some date</p>

          <p class="post__body">
            This card is only here so you can see the styling. Once your EJS
            loop is working, delete it and let the real posts fill this list.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — empty state

        When `posts` is empty, this list should be hidden and the block below
        shown instead. Use an if / else around the two blocks.
      -->
      <div class="empty">
        <div class="empty__emoji">🪶</div>
        <p>Nothing published yet</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/compose">Write the first one</a>
      </div>

      <p class="footnote">Built with Express · EJS · MongoDB</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
